# About this site

This is a Creestal site. It was scaffolded with `creestal new <%= @ctx.app_name %>`.

## Project layout

```
<%= @ctx.app_name %>/
  config.yml          ← site settings
  <%= @ctx.source %>/
    pages/            ← Markdown content, one file = one page
    layouts/          ← HTML templates that wrap your pages
    partials/         ← reusable HTML fragments (header, footer, …)
    assets/           ← CSS, JS, images — copied verbatim to output
  out/                ← generated site (gitignore this)
```

## The content model

Each file in `pages/` becomes one page in the output. Pages are written in Markdown with a YAML frontmatter block at the top:

```markdown
---
title: My page
date: 2026-01-01
---

# My page content
```

Creestal processes the Markdown, renders the matching Crinja layout, and writes a static HTML file to `out/`.

## Pages, layouts, and partials — how they connect

A page declares which layout to use via the `layout` frontmatter key (defaulting to whatever is set in `config.yml`).

The layout is an HTML file with Crinja expressions and include tags that tell Creestal where to put things:

- `{{ page.content }}` → rendered page content goes here
- `{% include "header.html" %}` → includes the `header.html` partial

Open `layouts/base.html` right now — you will see both in action.

